Notebook[{
Cell["One Postulate in Wolfram", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"e69a4948-d8ec-4e42-8cd3-ee12f14fde8c"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook is a public-facing computational companion to the local paper \
and Lean development. It follows the paper's argument closely enough that a \
reader can feel why one branch survives, while still keeping Lean as the \
proof authority.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eaeb1b6b-d4e2-484f-85d6-dc8ff8013a6b"],

Cell["What this notebook is for", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"93ccef60-464d-40d1-9966-860ffad99f39"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Question. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.1411764705882353, 0.3411764705882353, 0.6509803921568628]],
 "What is this notebook trying to make visible?"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1ef34b98-defb-4fb5-86b3-c34ded71e3cf"],

Cell["\<\
The goal is not to recreate every Lean proof step and not to turn the paper \
into a static summary card deck. The goal is to make the paper's dynamic \
claims visible: the kappa-dependent transformation law, the self-test \
supplied by the Killing form, the loss of a natural ruler at kappa = 0, and \
the emergence of finite invariant speed and Lorentzian causal structure only \
for kappa > 0.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7dc891fb-530f-4ec3-91b1-88c3b3224510"],

Cell["\<\
All mathematical and proof claims come from local repository files. Wolfram \
computes exact expressions and interactive views; the paper supplies the \
narrative; Lean supplies the proof authority.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f04fb6a-90a7-43b1-8fa6-8e8ba63ff2b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Answer. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.1803921568627451, 0.49019607843137253`, 0.42745098039215684`]],
 "This notebook is a computational companion: exact where it should be, \
public-facing in its presentation, and explicit about what belongs to \
Wolfram, to the paper, and to Lean."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"84cd5574-ecfa-4b39-b456-d79e924a34fc"],

Cell["The postulate", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4ad9d51c-552d-440e-85db-faff53364164"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Question. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.1411764705882353, 0.3411764705882353, 0.6509803921568628]],
 "What kind of explanation does the relativity principle allow?"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b5f02caf-30fe-41b6-b7cc-053df49726fc"],

Cell["\<\
Einstein's first postulate is treated here as a design principle: no hidden \
background structure should do the conceptual work that the symmetry rules \
themselves ought to do. The notebook therefore starts with the one-parameter \
family and delays geometric interpretation until the algebra has tested \
itself.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16c263e1-7de7-47fd-8da1-b807af17e05f"],

